# tools/ales_reverb_place_witness.rish — reverb_place: reverberate the master WET, then SEAT the reverberated result in the field — how WIDE it sits and WHERE, in one call (ALES214).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES214.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-125233_fill-ales214-lotus-reverb-place.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye (ALES191 — the named-room stereo wet, unchanged, its StereoReverbPresetError forwarded whole),
# lotus/stereo_width.rye (ALES211 — the width control, encode/scale-the-side/decode, run over the wet, its BadWidth reused), lotus/power.rye
# (ALES11 — the equal-power split split(pos, den), reused verbatim), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip and its proven gain), lotus/pan.rye
# (ALES10 — the StereoClip, its balance invariant, the fold bound max_pan_den), lotus/clock.rye (ALES5 — the validated sample clock). ALES212
# answered how wide (reverb_width); ALES213 answered where (reverb_pan); a keeper mixing a stereo master reaches for both at once, and reverb_place
# is that single seating — reverberate, then set the wet image's width AND position.
#
# lotus/reverb_place.rye composes three proven stages with NO new audio arithmetic: validate the width AND the pan first (a bad fraction refuses
# BadWidth or BadPan before the reverb writes, so the master is left DRY), reverberate wet in place (ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset, unchanged), set
# how wide (ALES211's stereo_width, the width proven legal so it cannot fault), place the wet image (ALES11's equal-power split feeding ALES2's proven
# gain on each channel, the pan proven legal so neither gain can fault). THE WIDTH-AT-CENTRE LAW: width == 0 with a centre pan folds the wet to mono
# (left == right), each channel an attenuation of the reverberated shared mid. THE PAN-AT-UNITY LAW: unity width keeps the wet's stereo image (the
# mid/side round-trip, <= 1 LSB per sample), a hard-left pan then routes the whole wash left, the right silenced. THE COMPOSITION LAW: a general
# width and off-centre pan equals the reverb then the width then the two equal-power gains byte for byte, each channel an attenuation of the widened
# wet. THE CENTRED-INVARIANT LAW: a centred master reverberates to a centred wet whose side is zero (width untouched), and a centre pan keeps left ==
# right, each attenuated below the wet. THE FAULT LAW: a bad width BadWidth, a bad pan BadPan, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range
# span BadRange, each leaving the master DRY and untouched.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_reverb_place_witness.rish

say "ales-reverb-place: Language EN — reverb_place reverberates a stereo master WET, then seats the reverberated result in the field with one call: how WIDE it sits (scaling the wet's side) and WHERE (scaling each wet channel by its equal-power weight). It fuses ALES212's how-wide and ALES213's where so a keeper seats the reverb return narrow-and-left or wide-and-centred in a single gesture. This proves three proven stages compose whole: reverb_place invents nothing, it orders."
say "ales-reverb-place: Style Radiant — the shape is stated positively as a composition of three proven stages with no new audio arithmetic: validate the width fraction and the pan fraction first (each refuses BadWidth or BadPan before the reverb ever writes, so a bad seating leaves the master fully dry), reverberate the master wet in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset unchanged, set how wide the wet sits through ALES211's stereo_width, then read ALES11's equal-power split for the proven-legal position and scale each wet channel by its weight through ALES2's proven gain. The edges name the two knobs honestly. width == 0 folds the wet to its shared mid (mono), and a centre pan then holds both channels equal below the pure wet; unity width keeps the wet's stereo image within one LSB, and a hard-left pan routes the whole wash left with the right silenced. Each pan weight is an attenuation no greater than the field denominator, so the placement seats the wash — it never amplifies."
say "ales-reverb-place: Lens TAME — one bounded i16 StereoClip transformed in place; the balance invariant is asserted on entry and exit, the clock is asserted valid, and BOTH fractions are bounded and checked BEFORE the reverb writes (width by ALES211's max_width_den 4096 / max_width_num 32768, pan by ALES11's max_pan_den 4096), so a bad width refuses BadWidth and a bad pan BadPan with the master dry — the atomicity crux, the prechecks precede the first write. The reverb then prechecks its own DurationTooLong / BadRange before writing; the width is proven legal so stereo_width cannot fault; each equal-power weight is proven <= den so both gains are attenuations whose saturate is a proven no-op, and the spans are the whole clip so neither gain can fault — a legal call refuses whole up front or completes whole. It reuses ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset, ALES211's stereo_width, ALES11's power.split, and ALES2's gain over their public APIs, inventing no new primitive; the width-at-centre law is proven mono and attenuated, the pan-at-unity law proven left-placed with the right silenced, the composition law proven byte for byte against the reverb then the width then the two equal-power gains with each channel an attenuation, the centred-invariant law proven identical and attenuated on a centred master; siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/reverb_place"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/reverb_place.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-reverb-place: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/reverb_place.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-reverb-place: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-reverb-place: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverb-place' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-reverb-place: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-reverb-place line"
